T157	Quotation 29084 29459	"I said nothing to him . . . nothing . . . I only said that there was no need to keep . . . too many labourers . . . if we could hire them by the day when we wanted them. You know . . . you know the labourers have been doing nothing for a whole week. . . . I. . . I. . . only said that, and he shouted and . . . said . . . a lot of horrible insulting things to me. What for?"
